From: TAK DM fix <tak-dm-fix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:10:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] TAK: DM routing, radio map controls, trails, stale cleanup
 (v0.12)

- v0.2: DMs go only to the recipient's node when known.
- v0.3: radio markers carry no TAK team (2525 friendly symbol).
- v0.4: radio picker and breadcrumb trails.
- v0.5: "Show on map" mode (radios + clients / clients only / clients +
  radios without a client).
- v0.6: remove radios not heard within a set time.
- v0.7: remove quiet TAK users (own setting); delete leftover radio markers
  (own radio, hidden, earlier runs) on enable/connect; trail minimum
  distance; keep trail dots forever (<archive/>); radio details gain
  "Last heard" and "Hops", trail dots carry SNR/hops; plain-language
  TAK server start error (port in use).
- v0.8: shortest trail interval is 1 minute (radios never report faster);
  saved 30-second settings act as 1 minute.
- v0.9: radio markers use plain friendly ground (a-f-G) instead of
  a-f-G-U-C, which ATAK labels CBT (combat).
- v0.12: built on v0.9 (one export button; the v0.10/v0.11 WinTAK export
  is dropped). The exported .pref declares XML 1.0: the XML library wrote
  version='1.1', which upstream's exact-match replace never caught.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X47yZwZ4Ze7N1MA9wkqGd9
